   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to an\nexemption for certain property from the prohibition of alcohol sales within a\ncertain distance of a church",
    "basePrintNo": "S8385",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8385-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8385\n\nSPONSOR: KAVANAGH\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to an\nexemption for certain property from the prohibition of alcohol sales\nwithin a certain distance of a church\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo amend the alcoholic Beverage Control Law by enabling an establishment\nlocated within two-hundred feet of a church to be eligible to apply for\na liquor license from the NYS Liquor Authority.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill amends subdivision 7 of section 64 of the Alco-\nhol Beverage Control law by adding a new paragraph describing the metes\nof the property at One Wall Street for the purposes of exempting such\npremises from the prohibition of holding a license within two hundred\nfeet of a church.\n\nSection two sets the effective date of the bill.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPrintemps America Inc is seeking to apply for an on-premise liquor,\nwine, beer and cider license for a location at One Wall Street/3 New\nStreet but is currently ineligible from applying due to the prohibition\nin subdivision 7 of section 64 of the Alcohol Beverage Control law,\nwhich stipulates that liquor licenses are prohibited from being issued\nwithin two hundred feet of a church. Printemps has consulted with and\ngained permission from the religious institution in question, Trinity\nChurch Wall Street, and has received unanimous conditional approval from\nManhattan Community Board 1 for a liquor license pursuant to meeting the\ncriteria outlined by the Community Board. Representatives of the Commu-\nnity Board have expressed that the Board has no objections to enactment\nof this bill. Based on these-considerations, this legislation seeks to\ngrant an exemption to subdivision 7 of section 64 of the Alcohol Bever-\nage Control law for Printemps America Inc for this location.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThis legislation will help generate sales, excise, and property tax\nrevenue.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
